Full text: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

Some files also hold the text of their book, cut into passages ("passageIndex"), and vectors computed from it. No right is
claimed on these texts. They come from Project Gutenberg, whose name and licence were removed from them:

- Lewis Carroll, Alice's Adventures in Wonderland (ebook 11).
- Edmond Rostand, Cyrano de Bergerac, translated by Gladys Thomas and Mary F. Guillemard (1898; ebook 1254).
- Gustave Flaubert, Madame Bovary, translated by Eleanor Marx-Aveling (ebook 2413).

Project Gutenberg gives them as being in the public domain in the United States. The length of copyright differs from one
country to another: check the law of yours before you reuse a text.

The code of LivingPaper, outside this folder, is under the AGPL-3.0 (see ../LICENSE).
